      "finding": "When the opposing rim big is off the floor, offenses slightly increase drives (+0.82 pp, t=3.3) and post-ups (+0.43 pp, t=2.4) and decrease three-point attempts (-1.79 pp, t=-5.8), but rim-share change is not significant (+0.12 pp, t=0.4) and overall PPP change is tiny (+0.008, t=1.1). With 1.07 M possessions the signal is described as WEAK/SMALL and insufficient to carry a paper."
