    "changed_decision": "yes",
    "explanation": "Without historical evidence, one might assume that any lineup change produces large shot-mix shifts that are trivially detectable. The results from SF34 show that even a clear defensive constraint (no rim big) yields only modest, partially null effects. This shifts the design toward a more rigorous causal framework, a composite significance test, and explicit power planning to avoid the weak/small failure seen in SF34. It also highlights multiplicity (SF26, SF-APPA-061) and measurement reliability (SF-TMP-018) as risks that must be mitigated."
